<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-primary mb-4">Common Causes of Painful Gum Swelling</h2>
</div>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Gumboil (Dental Abscess)</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A pus-filled swelling on the gum above or below a tooth, caused by infection of the dental pulp. The tooth may be tender to bite. Root canal or extraction eliminates the source. <a href="dental-abscess-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Dental abscess treatment</a> covers this in detail.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Periodontal Abscess</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacterial infection in an existing gum pocket. The gum swells acutely, is very tender, and may have pus discharge. Often triggered by food packing in deep pockets. See our <a href="bacterial-mouth-infection-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">bacterial mouth infection</a> page.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Pericoronitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Swelling and inflammation of the gum flap over a partially erupted tooth — most commonly a lower wisdom tooth. The gum tissue traps food and bacteria causing acute painful swelling that can spread to facial spaces.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Gingivitis with Acute Extension</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Severe gum inflammation that has extended into acute infection — red, swollen gums that bleed easily, with pus along the gum margins. Smoking and poor oral hygiene are common risk factors.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Necrotizing Ulcerative Gingivitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A painful, rapidly progressive gum infection with crater-like ulcers between teeth, gray tissue, and foul breath. Requires urgent debridement and antibiotics. <a href="pus-in-gums-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Pus in gums treatment</a> details this condition.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Traumatic Gum Injury</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Sharp food, dental appliances, or accidental bites can cause gum tears that become secondarily infected and swollen. Simple to manage if treated early.</p></div>
